thread:
jamie: Hey — ran into an issue after I bumped @redwood/sdk-js to v1.3.0. My TypeScript app calls client.summaries.create(...) but suddenly it's undefined and a direct curl to /v1/summaries returns 404. Anyone else hit this?

samir: Which exact SDK and API versions? can you paste package.json + minimal repro?

jamie: package.json: `
{
  "name": "notes-app",
  "dependencies": {
    "@redwood/sdk-js": "^1.3.0",
    "typescript": "4.9.5"
  }
}
`
node v18.14.0, ts-node for local testing. Repro (TS):
```ts
import Redwood from '@redwood/sdk-js';
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });
await client.summaries.create({
  model: 'open-7b',
  input: 'Summarize this meeting'
});
```
Result: in runtime client.summaries is undefined. I tried curl: `curl -X POST https://api.redwood.example.com/v1/summaries -H 'Authorization: Bearer $KEY' -d '{"input":"x"}' -w "%{http_code}\n"` -> returns `404`.

alex: Hmm — did you try inspecting the client object? `console.log(Object.keys(client))` to see available namespaces. Also, any proxy or corporate gateway? 404 from API suggests route removed or renamed at server side.

jamie: Yep did that: shows ["chat", "embeddings", "outputs"] — no summaries.

sdk-release-bot: Released @redwood/sdk-js v1.3.0 — breaking change: unifying output endpoints under `outputs.*` namespace; legacy `summaries.*` removed. See release notes: https://github.com/redwood/sdk-js/releases/tag/v1.3.0 :information_source:

samir: OK that matches. In v1.3 we migrated endpoints to outputs.create(...) with a `type`/`schema` body field instead of summaries.create. Example quick workaround:
```ts
await client.outputs.create({
  type: 'summary',
  model: 'open-7b',
  input: 'Summarize this meeting'
});
```
This should hit /v1/outputs and keep behavior. If you need the old names, pin to 1.2.8: `npm i @redwood/sdk-js@1.2.8` until your code is migrated.

jamie: Ah OK that explains it. We have a bunch of internal code calling summaries.create across microservices; need a migration plan. Is there an API compatibility shim we can use short-term?

liya: From platform: we can add a temporary server-side redirect for orgs on older SDKs, but that's a manual opt-in and we only keep it for 30 days. To get you on the list, we need exact org id + approximate traffic and which endpoints to shim. If you prefer not to change API, pin to 1.2.8 — that's lowest-effort.

samir: Also note another param rename: `response_format` -> `format` in the new outputs payload. If your callers pass old param names, server will ignore them (silently in some cases) -> unexpected responses. Check telemetry for failing requests.

jamie: Thanks. One other thing: some of our CI tests call the SDK directly and assume `summaries.create` exists. I'll file a PR to swap to outputs.create and add a small adapter shim in our code for now.

alex: For the support record: I'm creating an internal ticket to track this client break and document the migration steps + quicksearch for `summaries.create` across repos. Escalating to eng-platform to consider longer compatibility windows.

jamie: Appreciate it — please include our org (org-7342) for the temporary redirect list if platform agrees.

liya: Got it — added org-7342 to the request. Platform will reach out if they enable the shim. In the meantime pinning to 1.2.8 or switching to `client.outputs.create({type: 'summary', ...})` are the two paths. :thumbsup:
